{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Application data is kept under /srv/data on storage capable of filesystem snapshots.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An XFS logical volume was created and mounted at /srv/data, with persistent loop/LVM activation and mounting configured. The storage remained mounted and healthy after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2664d42ef4f24df7","cmd-fbe1a51d964d4ba4","cmd-46f7e4d108704db6"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Capture an earlier snapshot, then modify the directory so the live state diverges from that snapshot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The data_prechange LVM snapshot was directly observed with baseline hashes intact. Subsequent changes altered files and permissions, deleted a file and symlink, and added unwanted.tmp; baseline hash checks then failed as expected.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d65ae3f5f24441ee","cmd-5addc8580f394cdb"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Restore the exact content captured by the earlier snapshot after the modification.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The snapshot merge completed at 100%. After remounting, the recorded metadata matched exactly, every baseline file hash passed, the deleted symlink and original text were restored, and the post-snapshot file was absent.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dbb5285fa1844765","cmd-f7734043b2a74101"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation is established. Installing LVM, provisioning storage, creating test application data, snapshotting, modifying it, rolling it back, and configuring persistence all directly served the task. The failed initial snapshot attempt left incomplete LVM mappings, but it was a direct task attempt and its residue was explicitly diagnosed and removed before the successful snapshot; the temporary I/O probe was bounded and deleted. The unsuccessful btrfs-progs command showed no package installation or other confirmed mutation. Final lifecycle evidence shows no failed services, no new listening sockets, and healthy package-manager consistency.","evidence_ids":["cmd-42bc02bc74dd4c3b","cmd-73a38aebe2ed4e3a","cmd-1556decbe4024e6f","cmd-1f95d3cb01994c6f","cmd-28ebea0c8c5548e1","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence of snapshot creation, deliberate divergence, completed rollback, and exact content and metadata recovery. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, and service, storage, metadata, and data recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently agree with those identities.","limitations":["The exactness comparison relies on metadata and hash manifests generated by the executor before the snapshot rather than an independent verifier probe.","Lifecycle snapshots provide only bounded system-wide inventories and do not independently enumerate persistent task artifacts under /srv or /var/lib.","No cluster state was shown, but the managed topology contains only the standalone node1 and no cluster service was required."]}
